{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyrt1f52PA9kbiEjVcf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the integration and wrote the three causes and fixes in `ANSWER.md`. I tested it against a fake Intervals server I ran locally, not the real intervals.icu.\n\n**The three causes:**\n1. **Connect failed for everyone with 401.** The button was a plain link to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. Opening a link doesn't send the sign-in token, which only goes out on the app's own API calls, so the server rejected every click. Now the button sends an authenticated POST that returns `{authorize_url}`, and the browser then goes to that URL. GET on that path now returns 404.\n2. **Pasting the link by hand failed with 400 `invalid_request`.** The scope list asked for both `:READ` and `:WRITE` on ACTIVITY and CALENDAR. Intervals rejects an area named twice, because `:WRITE` already includes `:READ`. It's now `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`.\n   - The error doesn't say which parameter is wrong. I'm confident in this cause because the failures began when calendar sync shipped, the old working grant listed each area once, and changing `state` or `redirect_uri` gave the same error.\n   - Still, try one real authorize request with the new scopes before telling athletes it's fixed.\n3. **Rivera was told to reconnect after an hour.** Intervals tokens don't expire and come with no refresh token. The server assumed a one-hour lifetime anyway, and when the background refresher found nothing to refresh with, it marked the connection expired.\n   - Tokens without a stated expiry are now never expired by the server.\n   - When Intervals rejects a token with 401, the connection is marked `revoked, reconnect`.\n   - Rivera will need to connect once more, because their stored token was already discarded.\n\n**Test:** the full flow passed against the fake server: connect, the callback, wellness data loading, then a revoked token showing \"revoked, reconnect\" instead of an error.\n\n**The colleague's note:** the parts on no-expiry tokens, duplicate scopes and the init endpoint having to be a POST all applied. I didn't apply:\n- **Trimming the token request fields:** Rivera's connection succeeded with our current request, so it isn't a cause.\n- **Switching the state to a JWT:** the existing signed state already has a 15-minute limit.\n- **Guarding against reconnecting to a different account:** not related to these failures.\n- **Encrypting tokens at rest:** this dev server keeps everything in memory. It's still worth doing in production.\n\nThe changes are in `server.py`, `config.py` and `static/app.js`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2138,"cache_read_input_tokens":36260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2138},"output_tokens":707,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06435268-c4ce-4425-99e9-fbf8c605c1cf","uuid":"f3d5f733-a11d-49a9-94e2-b5bca421e862","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:49:56.370Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyrsmnCg1B9otwy8iyZ"}
